# L §5.14.3 (round 12b): a version that changes "the places of one of its legs (then even with δ = 0: the booked
# movement stays where it was booked, and the change is never silent)" creates an adjustment; E §5 step 4 "Record
# δ ≠ 0, or a leg whose places V changes (δ may be 0)". move_acct (known 2026-05-01) sends March's wage to konto2; the
# instance was booked on 2026-03-10 into konto and stays there (a: four wages in konto by April, none in konto2). Its
# adjustment has change 0.00 PLN (c) and nothing settles it, so konto's balance from 2026-05-01 is HOLE-CHANGED (b,
# L §8.1); no adjustment: line, since its remainder is 0 (E §5 step 5: "A remainder ≠ 0 at the cut is listed").
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source act "act"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind wages: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place konto2: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_amt: money PLN
input wage_dom: int
input pay_to: key accounts
def net[m in months]: money PLN = wage_amt at start_of(m)
def dest[m in months]: key accounts = pay_to at start_of(m)

move wage[m in months]: wages
  on day_of(m, wage_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to dest[m] amount net[m]

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  wage_amt = 5 000.00 PLN "umowa"
  wage_dom = 10 "umowa"
  pay_to = konto "umowa"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version move_acct
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-05-01
  replace pay_to = konto2 "aneks"

ask a: bal(konto, 2026-04-30), bal(konto2, 2026-04-30)
ask b: bal(konto, 2026-05-31)
ask c: count(x in adjustments over 2026), sum(x.change for x in adjustments over 2026)
=== expect
a: (20 000.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-03]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-04]
  cut 2026-10-20
b: ?"wage[2026-03] on 2026-03-10 changed after it was paid (version move_acct); is back pay due, and when?" (wage[2026-03])
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-03]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-04]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-05]
  cut 2026-10-20
c: (1, 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-10-20
